th="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Norman Kirk</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Norman Kirk was Prime Minister of New Zealand from 1972 until his death in office in 1974, leading the Third Labour Government.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/norman-manley"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/norman-manley.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Norman Manley</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Norman Manley was a Jamaican lawyer and statesman who founded the People's National Party in 1938, after the labour unrest of that year.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/normandy-landings"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/normandy-landings.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Normandy landings</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 1944</span><span class="enc-snip">The Normandy landings of 6 June 1944, known as D-Day, were the Allied amphibious and airborne invasion of German-occupied France that opened Operation Overlord.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/norn-language"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/norn-language.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Norn language</span><span class="enc-type">Term</span><span class="enc-snip">Norn was the North Germanic language spoken in Orkney, Shetland and Caithness, descended from the Old Norse of the Viking settlers.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/norodom-of-cambodia"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/norodom-of-cambodia.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Norodom of Cambodia</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Norodom was King of Cambodia from 1860 to 1904.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href