mg class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/north-africa.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">North Africa</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">North Africa is the region of Africa along the Mediterranean coast, including Egypt, Libya, Tunisia, Algeria and Morocco, bordered by the Sahara to the south.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/north-african-elephant"><span class="enc-name">North African elephant</span><span class="enc-type">Term</span><span class="enc-snip">The North African elephant was a population of elephants, now extinct, that lived in north-western Africa in antiquity.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/north-america"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/north-america.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">North America</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">North America is the continent comprising Canada, the United States, Mexico, Central America and the Caribbean.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/north-american-free-trade-agreement"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/north-american-free-trade-agreement.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">North American Free Trade Agreement</span><span class="enc-type">Event</span><span class="enc-snip">The North American Free Trade Agreement (NAFTA) was a treaty between Canada, Mexico and the United States that created one of the world's largest free trade areas.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/north-brabant"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/north-brabant.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">North Brabant</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">North Brabant is a province in the south of the Netherlands, with 's-Hertogenbosch as its